  READING T3: at 2-4 R_d a KURVS-like disc with gas at 2 R_d still has a RISING Newtonian curve (s_N > 0), so the MOND curve
  there is flat or rising and the point-mass estimator (which assumes s_N = -1) reads a0 -> infinity. Only near 6 R_d does the
  PM bias fall to ~0.1 dex (flat) / ~0.2 dex (rival), still with the rival's sign and gas-dependent. The shape-aware (DS) form
  removes the bias exactly for the right shape; its residual systematic is the unmeasured gas shape (d).

==============================================================================================================
T4  the pressure correction and the slope
==============================================================================================================
  observed V^2 = V_c^2 - P_true; the analyst reconstructs V_a^2 = V^2 + P_a.  With dP = P_a - P_true:
     s_a - s_c = (dP / V_a^2) (s_dP - s_c),  s_dP = dln dP/dlnR  (= 1 for k sigma^2 R/R_d with constant sigma).
  Kretschmer+2021: alpha(x) sigma^2 with x = R/R_e - 1; its log-slope is alpha'(x) (x+1)/alpha(x):
     R/R_e = 2 (R/R_d = 3.36): alpha = 2.533, dln(alpha)/dlnR = 0.720; k=2 equivalent alpha = 2 R/R_d = 6.72
     R/R_e = 3 (R/R_d = 5.04): alpha = 3.299, dln(alpha)/dlnR = 0.564; k=2 equivalent alpha = 2 R/R_d = 10.08
     R/R_e = 4 (R/R_d = 6.72): alpha = 3.773, dln(alpha)/dlnR = 0.348; k=2 equivalent alpha = 2 R/R_d = 13.44
  [PASS] T4a the slope-shift formula s_a - s_c = (dP/V_a^2)(1 - s_c) matches the numerical slope for every k-type pair (1e-5)
         measured: 195 pairs; max |diff| 6.7e-07

  pressure fraction f = P_k2/V_c^2 (truth k = 2) and V_obs/sigma, typical disc, mu 0.67, P2:
   flat  sigma   30: 2R_d f 0.20, V/sig 3.98 | 3R_d f 0.27, V/sig 4.03 | 4R_d f 0.35, V/sig 3.82 | 6R_d f 0.55, V/sig 3.15
   flat  sigma   45: 2R_d f 0.45, V/sig 2.19 | 3R_d f 0.61, V/sig 1.97 | 4R_d f 0.80, V/sig 1.43 | 6R_d pressure-dominated (V_c^2 < P)
