  READING T4: a mis-specified pressure term moves s by (dP/V_a^2)(1 - s_c); an OVER-correction (truth weaker than k = 2)
  steepens the reconstructed curve upward and reads as a LARGER a0 (the rival's direction); an under-correction the reverse.
  sigma-gradient: with a local sigma(R) ~ R^gamma in k sigma^2 R/R_d the pressure term's own slope is 1 + 2 gamma instead of 1.

