  READING T5: a coherent slope error of about +0.1 is the entire separation of the two laws at KURVS radii. The point-mass bias
  (T3, 0.1 to >1 dex) and a mis-specified pressure term (T4) are each of that size or larger, so the estimator needs the
  baryon SHAPE (gas extent) and the pressure prescription controlled to ~0.05 in slope before the stack can separate the laws.

